course: dictionary
lesson: 4645
title: What is a historian?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A historian is a person who studies the past. Historians find out what happened long ago by looking at evidence such as documents, objects and buildings. They do not just guess. They check their evidence carefully before they say what is true.
explain: You can be a historian too. In history lessons you «think like historians»: you ask who made a source, why they made it, and whether another source says the same thing. Pupils who do this become better at spotting what is true.
explain: Some stories are not true, even if people tell them for a long time. «A good historian says which is which» means a historian sorts real facts from legends and fantasy. «Historians believe» tells you what most experts think, based on the evidence.
fact: A historian is a person who studies history and writes about the past.
fact: Historians use evidence such as documents, objects and buildings.
fact: «Historians believe» means most experts think this is true, based on the evidence.
fact: A good historian checks extra claims, such as a story about paper-making, against other evidence.
fact: Some stories, like the wooden horse of Troy, are legends, and a historian says so.
exercise: «Some historians doubt the experiment happened as told.» What does doubt mean here? | Are sure to forget it | Are certain it is true | *Think it may not be true | Want to repeat it
exercise: What does a historian do? | Invents stories about dragons and kites | Predicts the weather for next week | Sells old objects in a shop | *Studies the past and writes about it, using evidence
exercise: Pupils ask who made a source and why. What is this called in history lessons? | Thinking like dragons | *Thinking like historians | Thinking like weather forecasters | Thinking like kites
test: Which of these is a legend, not a fact, according to the lesson? | Porcelain | *The Minotaur | Tea | Kites
test: Why do historians check a source against other evidence? | To make it look old | To make it longer | To hide it from others | *To see whether it is true
exam: What is the name for a person who studies the past using evidence? | Inventor | Weather forecaster | Scientist | *Historian
